# BAS I-Case3 three-arm narrowing: after the Int arm, remaining_scrutinee becomes
# scrutinee ∩ ~Int (Negation accumulation). After the Str arm it becomes
# scrutinee ∩ ~Int ∩ ~Str. The wildcard arm sees the fully narrowed remaining type.
# normalize_intersection handles the negation accumulation correctly.
[describe: [fn [let x]
  [match x
    Int:  "integer"
    Str:  "string"
    ...:  "other"]]
 r1: [describe 42]
 r2: [describe "hello"]
 r3: [describe True]]
=== out
Dict({"describe": Function(x), "r1": String("integer"), "r2": String("string"), "r3": String("other")})
